## Zero-trust model

Every action an agent takes must be explicitly allowed by its `Policy`.
Anything not on the allowlist is denied:

```python
from {{ package_name }} import Agent, Policy

agent = Agent("example", Policy(allowed_actions=frozenset({"read:config"})))
agent.authorize("read:config")   # ok
agent.authorize("write:config")  # raises PermissionDeniedError
```

